\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Latvian cbank wants 1999 deficit lowered. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Martinsh Gravitis \par \uc2 493 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 1999\par 13:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  RIGA, Aug 11 (Reuters) - Latvia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday urged the government to take steps to limit the 1999 fiscal deficit but said the lat \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  faced no devaluation threat, despite its recent weakness caused by budget woes. \par \par \uc2  Parliament last week passed a 27.95 million lat package of spending cuts to the 1999 budget. The cuts were half what the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had said were needed and will still leave the budget with a deficit of 3.5 percent of planned 1999 GDP. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would urge the government to make any necessary steps to reduce the fiscal deficit below three percent (of GDP) this year," Bank of Latvia President Einars Repshe told a news conference. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Edmunds Krastinsh told Reuters the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fiscal deficit target was possible but depended on a recovery in tax revenues in the second half. \par \par \uc2  "If the economy picks up and revenues improve, it is possible. To come to three percent we would need to generate additional 20 million lats or so during the remaining five months," Krastinsh said. \par \par \uc2  Budget deficit worries, mostly on the retail level, forced the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time this year on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market last month as the late weakened against the SDR world \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket it is pegged to. \par \par \uc2  In recent days dealers have seen more signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a weak dollar abroad fed fresh greenback demand and then Russia's political crisis further weakened lat sentiment. It was again soft on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar/lat is at the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band. It's been hovering there all day so probably the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is in the market (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 )," said one dealer. \par \par \uc2  However, Repshe said there was no threat of devaluation and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could defend it if necessary. \par \par \uc2  "There is no devaluation risk and it will not be allowed, either now or in the forseeable future. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has both the political will and sufficient resources to do that, with lat coverage at 114 percent," Repshe said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said markets took last week's cuts as a sign of more to come and would be disappointed if the government did not tighten further. \par \par \uc2  "To (stabilise) the market and to take pressure off the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  then it would be wise to adjust these spending cuts a little bit more," said Raymond Beimers, an economist with ABN Amro. \par \par \uc2  "Being such a small country with a lot of other imbalances it would be wise to have the deficit at (most) at three percent of GDP but even less would be better," said Beimers. \par \par \uc2  Latvia's economy was pushed into a recession after the Russian rouble devaluation last August cut it off from its mainstay market, squeezing tax revenues and forcing the government into budget cuts. \par \par \uc2  ((Riga Newsroom +371 722 2079, reuters@reuters.lv)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv8b02s2e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
