\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Latvian  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes \highlight\uc2  again. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Burton Frierson \par \uc2 458 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juli 1999\par 13:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  RIGA, July 23 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the fourth day in a row to support the lat, which remained weak amid budget deficit worries despite government plans for large spending cuts to bolster the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  However, analysts said the lat was not in imminent danger of devaluation. They expected finance ministry plans for about 50 million lats ($84 million) in spending cuts in the 1999 budget eventually to reassure the market. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer Karlis Bauze told Reuters the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2  had again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday to keep the lat in its corridor after entering the market for the first time this year on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "Yes, we did (enter the market)...We did one small \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  but it was very light." \par \par \uc2  The lat is pegged at 0.7997 lats to the SDR, the IMF's world basket \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and is allowed to fluctuate in a band of one percent either side. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not generally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  while the lat remains safely within its corridor, but steps in more or less automatically when it threatens to leave its fluctuation band. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Edmunds Krastinsh told Latvian Radio that the government was eying some 50 million lats in spending cuts which would "affect almost all branches". \par \par \uc2  He said the 1999 budget deficit would be between three and five percent of GDP, depending on privatisation revenue. \par \par \uc2  The new government, which took over last week after the previous one resigned amid criticism of its handling of the budget, has pledged to cut the deficit to shore up the lat's economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  Krastinsh also said Latvia expected to tap international debt markets next year, and would base its 2000 budget conservatively on expectations of 3.5 percent GDP growth and 3.0 percent inflation. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said it remained to be seen whether the government would have to cut more than 50 million lats in expenditure. \par \par \uc2  "In this turbulent situation I'd say this was quite a good introductory step and perhaps the government will follow with even more if the markets push them to do so...(but) the absolute levels of borrowing are relatively low even compared to some emerging markets," said Hansabank Markets analyst Urmas Riel. \par \par \uc2  "At least the trend should be well received by the markets." \par \par \uc2  But dealers said it would take time for the news to bolster the lat. \par \par \uc2  "Generally (lat \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) is not over yet, but of course the amounts are small, it's mainly local market demand, no international demand," said Janis Strazinskis, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer with Vereinsbank. \par \par \uc2  ($1 = 0.5974 Latvian lats) \par \par \uc2  ((Riga Newsroom +371 722 2079, reuters@reuters.lv)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7n03uwh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
