\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS- \highlight22\uc2 Latvia \highlight\uc2  cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  again,firm stand seen. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Burton Frierson \par \uc2 587 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juli 1999\par 12:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  RIGA, July 21 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market to support the lat for the second day in a row on Wednesday and analysts said they expected officials go all the way to defend a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakening amid budget woes. \par \par \uc2  However, some analysts said officials, despite their resolve to the defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , may be fighting a lost cause if government efforts to sort out the state's finances fail to woo market sentiment back to the lat. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer Karlis Bauze said the bank had again bought lats on Wednesday after entering the market for the first time this year on Tuesday, as the market's offered lat rates weakened below the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels. \par \par \uc2  "Yes, we did small deals this morning but I would say really light...it is passive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but in small amounts," Bauze, told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  The lat scraped the bottom of its plus/minus one percent fluctuation band against the SDR basket of world \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which it is pegged to at 0.7997, in early Wednesday trade. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At 1025 GMT the dollar was at 0.6011 to the lat\tab   on the market's offer side, sitting on top of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's offered rate. The lat closed at 0.6012 against the dollar on Tuesday. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  does not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  actively to support the lat, but it acts as a supplier of last resort in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  when market rates overshoot either side of the fluctuation band.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par It does not disclose the levels at which it \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  but its offered rates represent the widest points in the band.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last year amid worries over the the Russian crisis and was forced to enter the market now due to market concerns over a poor economy and gaping budget deficit.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par New pro-business Prime Minister Andris Shkele took over last week after his predecessor, Vilis Krishtopans, resigned amid sharp criticism over his handling of the budget and has pledged budget cuts to shore up the lat's economic foundation.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "They seem to be very concerned about the budget and it looks like they are determined to do something about it...I don't see them devaluing," said Deutsche Bank analyst Chris Blevins.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "If they devalued imports would become much more expensive and Latvia is in the transition period where they're updating infrastructure, industrial complex and so-forth, therefore devaluing would very much hurt that effort," Blevins added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Devaluation would force painful \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate hikes to combat inflation, which is currently subdued.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts also said the government would put itself in a bigger bind by devaluing, which would raise the cost of service foreign debt like the 150 million euro bond it launched in May.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, other analysts said the markets may have already decided that Latvia's economy will not mend itself without a devaluation to revive exports to Russia, once its mainstay market until it dried up last year after the rouble devaluation.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I don't think necessarily it has to happen but on the other hand if (devaluation) did happen it would not be really surprising," said Handelsbanken analyst Gunnar Tersman.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It would be a natural reaction to the situation they are in with a weak economy...and budget problems and all of these things, all of them related to the Russian crisis." ((Riga Newsroom +371 722 2079, reuters@reuters.lv)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7l0460r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
