\par\par \b \uc2  Latvian cbank again buying lats on  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  market. \b0\par\par\uc2 265 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juli 1999\par 10:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  RIGA, July 21 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  passively again on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  "Yes, we did small deals this morning but I would say really light...it is passive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but in small amounts," Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer Karlis Bauze told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Latvia entered the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the first time this year on Tuesday as the lat sagged against the dollar amid worries over the economy and the budget deficit. \par \par \uc2  At 0800 GMT the market's offered dollar rate was 0.6016 against the lat and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate was 0.6013. \par \par \uc2  The lat is pegged to the SDR basket of world \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 0.7997 and fluctuates in a band of plus/minus one percent. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  actively to support the lat, but it acts as a supplier of last resort in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  when market rates overshoot either side of the fluctuation band. \par \par \uc2  It does not disclose the levels at which it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's offered rates represent widest points in the band. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year, as the lat sagged amid worries over the effects of the Russian economic crisis, and raised interest rates to protect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  This year it has gradually relaxed rates in a bid to revive the money market, which all but dried up after the Russian crisis struck last August. \par \par \uc2  ((Burton Frierson, Riga Newsroom +371 722 2079, reuters@reuters.lv)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7l045tj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
