\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS- \highlight22\uc2 Latvia \highlight\uc2  cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  for second day. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Burton Frierson \par \uc2 544 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juli 1999\par 13:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  RIGA, July 21 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market to support the lat for the second day in a row on Wednesday and analysts said they expected the government to go all out to tackle the budget woes underming the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer Karlis Bauze said the bank had again bought lats on Wednesday after entering the market for the first time this year on Tuesday, as lat rates in the market weakened below the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels. \par \par \uc2  "Yes, we did small deals this morning but I would say really light... It is passive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but in small amounts," Bauze told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  The lat scraped the bottom of its plus/minus one percent fluctuation band against the SDR basket of world \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which it is pegged to at 0.7997, in early Wednesday trade. \par \par \uc2  At 1025 GMT the dollar was at 0.6011 to the lat LATU) on the market's offer side, above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's offered rate. The lat closed at 0.6012 against the dollar on Tuesday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  actively to support the lat, but it acts as a supplier of last resort when market rates overshoot either side of the fluctuation band. \par \par \uc2  It does not disclose the levels at which it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  but its offered rates represent the widest points in the band. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year amid worries over the Russian crisis, was forced to support the lat due to the market's concerns over the poor economy and a gaping budget deficit. \par \par \uc2  Pro-business Prime Minister Andris Shkele, who took over last week after his predecessor Vilis Krishtopans resigned amid sharp criticism over his handling of the budget, has pledged budget cuts to shore up the lat's economic foundations. \par \par \uc2  "They seem to be very concerned about the budget and it looks like they are determined to do something about it... I don't see them devaluing," said Deutsche Bank analyst Chris Blevins. \par \par \uc2  "If they devalued imports would become much more expensive and Latvia is in the transition period where they're updating infrastructure, industrial complex and so-forth, therefore devaluing would very much hurt that effort," Blevins added. \par \par \uc2  Devaluation could also lead to painful \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate hikes to combat inflation, which is currently subdued. \par \par \uc2  Analysts also said the government would put itself in a bigger bind by devaluing, which would raise the cost of servicing foreign debt such as a 150 million euro ($156.9 million) bond it launched in May. \par \par \uc2  However, other analysts said the market may have already decided that Latvia's economy will not mend itself without a devaluation to revive exports to Russia, once its mainstay market until it dried up last year after the rouble devaluation. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think necessarily it has to happen but on the other hand if (devaluation) did happen it would not be really surprising," said Handelsbanken analyst Gunnar Tersman. \par \par \uc2  "It would be a natural reaction to the situation they are in with a weak economy...and budget problems and all of these things, all of them related to the Russian crisis." \par \par \uc2  ($1=.9557 Euro). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7l03xut\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
