\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Latvian cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to support weak lat. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Burton Frierson \par \uc2 498 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juli 1999\par 14:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  RIGA, July 20 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  entered the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the first time this year on Tuesday as the lat sagged and analysts said the new government needed to act quickly on a gaping budget deficit to shore up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar opened at 0.6020 to the lat, continuing a soft trend before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 0.6012, dealers said. At 1235 GMT the offered dollar rate was 0.6007 against the lat. \par \par \uc2  "Yes, we did (enter the market)...but this is passive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . This means that it is much cheaper for banks to buy dollars from us, not other banks," Bank of Latvia \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer Karlis Bauze told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  Latvia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not enter the market actively to support the lat, which is pegged to the SDR basket of world \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 0.7997 and fluctuates against it in a plus/minus one percent band. \par \par \uc2  It does regularly offer rates at the end of the fluctuation band as a last resort for banks. Last August, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market to support the lat during the Russian financial crisis. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said it was the first time this year the Bank of Latvia had entered the market and blamed worries over the budget deficit and an economic slump. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not say at what level banks began selling them lats. \par \par \uc2  "Mainly I think it is the bad macroeconomic situation and the bad situation with the budget," said Martinsh Strazds, a dealer with Unibanka, although he said dollar demand was not aggressive and trade was slow. \par \par \uc2  Latvia's economy contracted by 2.3 percent in the first quarter after shrinking by 1.9 percent in the last three months of 1998 due to the effects of Russia's crisis. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say there is little the government can do to stimulate growth until the Russian export market, the mainstay of Latvian producers until last year's rouble devaluation, recovers or Western Europe sees a growth spurt. \par \par \uc2  It can cut the budget deficit, which widened to 47.5 million lats from a 29.2 million lat shortfall at the end of May. The last government was seen struggling to keep it under three percent of GDP to keep Latvia's EU hopes alive. \par \par \uc2  "If they really want to avoid a devaluation...they have to demonstrate to the markets that they are serious in keeping their economy in balance and that would necessitate budget cuts and it would also require that authorities can accept higher unemployment," said Handelsbanken analyst Gunnar Tersman. \par \par \uc2  New Prime Minister Andris Shkele, who took over last week after Vilis Krishtopans resigned amid sharp criticism over his handling of the economy, has said the top priority of his cabinet would be to begin putting the state's finances back in order. \par \par \uc2  ((Riga Newsroom +371 722 2079, reuters@reuters.lv)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7k043hw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
