\par\par \b \uc2  LATVIAN O/N RATES CLIMB, DOLLAR UP VS LAT. \b0\par\par\uc2 225 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 September 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  RIGA, Sept 23 (Reuter) - Latvian overnight rates climbed on Tuesday and were seen rising further as banks borrow to meet their monthly reserve requirments, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  In \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, the dollar jumped late Monday on a surge of strong demand but brokers could not say who was behind the deals or why. \par \par \uc2  Overnight rates rose on Tuesday to a bid/ask range of 2.30/3.00 percent from 2.0 to 2.50 percent after hardly moving last week. \par \par \uc2  "There is a lot more activity on the market this week and the rates should continue to climb," said Maris Vinklers of Hansabank Markets' interest rate products department. \par \par \uc2  He added that banks were now borrowing to meet the reserve requirements of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, a late Monday order pushed the dollar up against the lat. \par \par \uc2  The lat eased against the dollar late Monday to 0.5846/51 from 0.5825/35 and held steady there on Tuesday morning. The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate was 0.5824. \par \par \uc2  Dealers were at a loss to explain the sudden order for dollars but said morning trade was quiet. \par \par \uc2  "Activity is down this morning," said Andris Savickis, a dealer with Rigas komercbanka. \par \par \uc2  -- Ed Stoddard, Riga newsroom +371 721 52 40 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020040131dt9n00hfh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
