\par\par \b \uc2  LATVIA-O/N RATES UP AHEAD OF WEEKEND, LAT SEEN EASING. \b0\par\par\uc2 201 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juli 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  RIGA, July 11 (Reuter) - Overnight rates rose ahead of the weekend and the lat/dollar rate came close to the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate on Friday. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said that the lat was expected to ease slightly in response to local market demand for dollars. \par \par \uc2  Volumes on both markets were relatively low because of the summer holiday, dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Overnight rates climbed to a bid/ask of 4.00/4.50 percent on Friday from 3.20/4.20 percent on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said rates usually rise ahead of the weekend as banks have three days to meet their reserve requirements and expected them to fall next week. \par \par \uc2  In \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, the interbank lat/dollar rate was steady at 0.5699/704, near the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate of 0.5696/811. \par \par \uc2  "This situation won't last as we don't expect banks to sell dollars to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...There is a big order for dollars from a couple of sources right now," said one dealer. \par \par \uc2  Dealers declined to name the source. \par \par \uc2  -- Ed Stoddard, Riga newsroom +371 721 52 40 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020040131dt7b003kl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
