\par\par \b \uc2  LATVIAN OVERNIGHT RATES STAY LOW, DEALERS EYE EU SUMMIT. \b0\par\par\uc2 195 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juni 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  RIGA, June 16 (Reuter) - Overnight rates remained low in Latvia as the liquidity situation in the banks remained healthy, dealers said on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that overnight rates were at the same levels as Friday's 1.75 percent to 2.75 percent. \par \par \uc2  "There are more lenders than borrowers right now...banks do not seem concerned about their liquidity situation and their obligations to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Maris Vinklers, head of money markets at Hansabank-Latvija. \par \par \uc2  He added that rates were expected to remain low for the rest of the month. \par \par \uc2  The lat was trading against the dollar near the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Latvia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate of 0.5706 in a range of 0.5709 to 0.5713, almost the same level as Friday. \par \par \uc2  "There are a lot of investments coming into Latvia now, and so there is a big demand for lats," said one dealer. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar could gain against the lat, depending on the outcome of the EU summit in Amsterdam and its impact on European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the dealer added. \par \par \uc2  -- Ed Stoddard, Riga newsroom +371 721 52 40 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020040130dt6g01b2r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
